  8: 
  9: ## Guild creation:
 10: https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ed5daea2-f9fd-4370-a884-442dfa20843a
 11: 
 12: ## Translation system:
 13: https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/fb16b2db-ec7a-4060-bf26-f0d8cf7d95be
 14: 
 15: ## Item upgrades and new effects:
 16: https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/465fa86a-1a7b-4c26-9794-aba5297c5e19
 17: 
 18: ## Emote wheel:
 19: https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/35c67fab-1c7c-4c41-b5a0-97cc0c90fd6a
 20: 
 21: 
 22: Client for OpenMU made in BabylonJS based of afrokick's JSClient, the client is being developed to work with any version available and connect on the go to different servers either stored in this repo's serverlist.md or added manually to the list.
 23: 
 24: 
 25: Current working ~somewhat version is S6EP3; 0.97d ships beside it (tag V097D) and more are to be added down the line.
 26: 
 27: ## Installing
 28: 
 29: Needs [Docker Desktop](https://www.docker.com/products/docker-desktop/) and
 30: [Bun](https://bun.sh) ≥ 1.0.
 31: 
 32: ### 1. The server
 33: 
 34: ```bash
 35: git clone https://github.com/MUnique/OpenMU.git
 36: cd OpenMU/deploy/all-in-one
 37: ```
 38: 
 39: To use the official docker image of OpenMU, run:
 40: 
 41: ```bash
 42: docker compose up -d --no-build
 43: ```
 44: 
 45: OpenMU's admin panel comes up on <http://localhost:80>. Create an account there before logging in.
 46: 
 47: ### 2. The client
 48: 
 49: ```bash
 50: bun install
 51: bun run dev        # http://localhost:5173/online
 52: bun run proxy      # ws<->tcp bridge, in a second shell
 53: ```
 54: 
 55: The proxy is not optional: a browser cannot open a TCP socket, so every packet to OpenMU goes
 56: through it. Run it next to the client.
 57: 
 58: The proxy also carries the band system (instruments played live): those frames never reach
 59: OpenMU, the proxy relays them to the players who can see the performer. `BAND=off` disables
 60: it, `BAND_MAX_PERFORMERS` (16) and `BAND_MAX_RECEIVERS` (48) cap it, and it needs `TRACK`
 61: on. It logs a `band: {...}` stats line once a minute when something happened.
 62: 
 63: **No server, no Docker?** `bun run dev` and open <http://localhost:5173/offline> for the
 64: single-player offline demo.
 65: 
 66: 
 67: ```
